Package: DSEMr
Title: Bayesian Dynamic Structural Equation Modeling
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Marcus", "Harris", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "marcus.harris.uconn@gmail.com"),
    person("The extendr contributors", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Authors of vendored Rust crates; see inst/AUTHORS")
  )
Description: Specifies, simulates, and estimates Bayesian dynamic structural
    equation models (DSEM) for intensive longitudinal and time-series data using
    an offline-vendored 'Rust' backend and an R reference engine. Models compile
    from extended 'lavaan' formulas or section-based SEM scripts into a unified
    intermediate representation supporting single-level autoregressive, residual
    dynamic (Asparouhov and Muthen, 2020, <doi:10.1080/10705511.2019.1626733>),
    continuous-time Ornstein-Uhlenbeck (Oud and Jansen, 2000,
    <doi:10.1007/BF02294374>), dynamic factor, binary or ordinal probit, and
    Tobit censored models; two-level location-scale, exact collapsed ARMA(1,1),
    random residual covariance, and multivariate dynamic models (Asparouhov,
    Hamaker, and Muthen, 2018, <doi:10.1080/10705511.2017.1406803>; McNeish and
    Hamaker, 2020, <doi:10.1037/met0000250>); three-level and cross-classified
    dynamic models; time-interval grid alignment; standardized estimates and
    Bayesian R-squared (Schuurman, Ferrer, de Boer-Sonnenschein, and Hamaker,
    2016, <doi:10.1037/met0000062>); posterior partial correlations, hypothesis
    and Wald tests, impulse response functions, DIC model comparison, APA
    tables, LaTeX equations, path diagrams, Monte Carlo studies, and an
    optional 'shiny' studio.
